# BitBake / Yocto conventions (Scarthgap)

- Every recipe: `SUMMARY`, `LICENSE`, `LIC_FILES_CHKSUM`, and a pinned `SRCREV` for git sources (no `${AUTOREV}`).
- Filenames: `<name>_<version>.bb`; appends: `<name>_%.bbappend` only when version-agnostic is intended.
- Use override syntax `VAR:append = " item"` (leading space) and `VAR:remove`; never the old `_append`.
- Prefer `?=` / `??=` in conf snippets so local overrides still work; explain the difference when used.
- Add files with `FILESEXTRAPATHS:prepend := "${THISDIR}/files:"` in bbappends.
- Kernel changes: config fragments (`*.cfg`) added via `SRC_URI += "file://name.cfg"` in a `linux-raspberrypi_%.bbappend` — not a full defconfig replacement.
- Image recipes `inherit core-image` and use `IMAGE_INSTALL:append` / `IMAGE_FEATURES`.
- Security-relevant settings (users, ssh, read-only-rootfs, debug-tweaks) get a one-line comment explaining the risk they address.
- `layer.conf` must set `LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_secure-pi5 = "scarthgap"`.
